    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_427b2fe3d3dc7ef4b5f7189b68c35e08a4cd33630abe7c3988410300beccca2e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Functional-equation parity becomes active analytic input in both GL2 aspects. In the weight aspect, restricting weights modulo four changes the parity-sensitive Bessel average and gives opposite signs to the surviving off-diagonal Fourier tail. In the prime-level aspect, the sign projector inserts the coefficient lambda_f(N), changes the Petersson correlation and Kloosterman factorization, and again reverses the tail correction, refining the shared orthogonal density into SO(even) and SO(odd).",
