    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_428036cfda946b09b6288f6355230993b17d4e9b0dbdc99efb12d86b922dadfe",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Fourier support acts as a source-specific arithmetic aperture: through the explicit formula it bounds the prime ranges that enter the density calculation, and beyond support one the parity-split GL2 and symmetric-square arguments must evaluate family-sensitive off-diagonal structure rather than rely only on the diagonal. In the weight and level GL2 aspects those evaluations produce sign-dependent orthogonal Fourier tails, while the symmetric-square calculation reaches its symplectic correction by a different Poisson-and-boundary mechanism.",
