    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c75fafe2bf160f9a80695a5cc637255d20e5c2cc2fa5e094a3d82462e8bfe129",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Both aspects use a controlled change of measure to pass from the inverse symmetric-square weights built into Petersson averaging to uniform family sums. In the weight aspect the uniform statistic is written as a harmonic average multiplied by L(1,sym^2 f), which GRH permits replacing by a short coefficient series; in the level aspect the inverse harmonic weight omega_f^{-1} is likewise truncated to a short sum of lambda_f(n^2)/n before Petersson is applied.",
