    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e24b13f1eec8d957829fc928c51c49ad2604b3be454b2f549d2c8ecb13a4dafc",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source carries arithmetic density information through a full optimization pipeline. Beyond-diagonal analysis yields nonconstant Fourier-side corrections for the sign-specific orthogonal and symplectic kernels; positivity and normalization turn their one-level densities into constrained detectors of central vanishing; Ahiezer-Paley-Wiener factorization and Plancherel convert the detector problem to a quadratic form for a compact convolution operator; and the Fredholm minimizer adapts the test to the kernel, improving the resulting arithmetic bounds over squared sinc.",
