    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_fa278e712f0294f588e23e9b6f74a2c2379d29df2367bf2b357f33413d87b624",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source gives a conditional detector chain from classical prime cancellation to higher-degree zero geometry. Hypothesis 4 controls the new oscillatory prime-in-progression term that appears when Fourier support is enlarged beyond the earlier range, extending the parity-mixed density theorem to support inside (-7/3,7/3); a nonnegative squared-sinc test then makes any real off-line zero contribute hyperbolic growth incompatible with the averaged bound, yielding the endpoint beta at most 13/14.",
